      en: "Boa Vista, the easternmost island of Cape Verde, is characterized by vast white sand deserts, dunes, and turquoise waters. It is a key nesting site for loggerhead sea turtles. The island's economy relies on tourism, salt extraction, and fishing. Sal Rei, the main town, features colorful colonial buildings. Boa Vista is also known for its music festivals and traditional pottery.",
